course: dictionary
lesson: 11453
title: Words for judging
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who makes a decision and how they make it. Adjudication is one of these words. Look for the clues: a judge or a person in charge, and both sides of an argument.
explain: «The judge listened to both teams before the adjudication was made.» The clues are judge, listened and both teams, so adjudication must be the final decision. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The judge listened to both teams before the decision was made." It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Adjudication can also mean the act of judging a contest. «The adjudication of the singing competition took all afternoon.» Here the clues are singing and competition, so it means the judging of the contest, not a court case.
fact: Adjudication is a noun, so it names a thing: a decision, or the act of judging.
fact: «Adjudication» means the official decision made by a judge or another person in charge, after hearing both sides.
fact: «Adjudication» can also mean the act of judging a contest, such as a music, dance or debate competition.
fact: Adjudication is often heard in law, in eisteddfods, at music festivals and in debating.
fact: Phrases like «under adjudication» mean a matter is still being decided, and «final adjudication» means the last decision.
exercise: «The judge's adjudication settled the argument between the two neighbours.» What does adjudication mean here? | *The official decision made after hearing both sides | A picnic with friends | A loud shout in the street | A long walk in the park
exercise: «The adjudication panel gave Sam the top mark for his song.» What does adjudication most likely describe? | *Judging the singing competition | Losing a football match | Cooking dinner | Painting a fence
exercise: Priya says adjudication is just a fancy word for a party. What is the correct meaning? | *A decision made by a judge after hearing both sides | A school trip to the museum | A quiet rest after lunch | A party with games and music
test: «The debate ended, and the adjudication was read out to the teams.» What was read out? | The team lists | *The judge's decision on who won | The weather forecast
test: «The school's new rule is still under adjudication.» What does this suggest? | It is a sports rule | It has been finished and forgotten | *It is still being decided | It was painted blue
exam: Which phrase shows the last, final decision? | under adjudication | a music festival | the adjudication panel | *final adjudication
